WEBVTT

00:00:01.020 --> 00:00:02.980
<i>Why is this happening to me?</i>

00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:06.190
<i>I'm in love with your best friend, Taiyo Oga!</i>

00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:08.690
<i>I'm in love with your best friend, Sun-chan!</i>

00:00:08.940 --> 00:00:11.690
<i>The mother of all double confessions of love!
And then...</i>

00:00:12.030 --> 00:00:14.450
<i>I'm looking forward
to spending time with you, Joro.</i>

00:00:14.450 --> 00:00:17.370
<i>...a demonic stalker appeared!</i>

00:01:51.040 --> 00:01:53.590
EPISODE 02
I'M ATTACKED BY
AN IMPOSSIBLE SPIRAL

00:01:51.590 --> 00:01:55.710
Sheesh. It's sad that I have to give up
my precious lunchtime.

00:01:54.210 --> 00:01:58.090
LIBRARY

00:01:59.090 --> 00:02:05.810
CHECK-OUT

00:02:00.140 --> 00:02:01.890
Hello, Joro.

00:02:01.890 --> 00:02:03.760
I'm delighted you came again.

00:02:13.110 --> 00:02:14.940
I hate people who are mean.

00:02:14.940 --> 00:02:16.780
I hate people who threaten me.

00:02:16.780 --> 00:02:21.910
Then you won't want me by your side,
so I'll just tell Oga all of your secrets.

00:02:21.910 --> 00:02:23.910
Don't get the wrong idea!

00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:26.000
I'm fine having you sit next to me.

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:29.000
Oh, you run so hot and cold!

00:02:30.580 --> 00:02:32.170
So let's talk.

00:02:32.540 --> 00:02:37.010
First I'd like you to tell me
how you're helping those two.

00:02:39.930 --> 00:02:41.010
I want you to tell me.

00:02:42.970 --> 00:02:45.680
Fine. Um...

00:02:46.020 --> 00:02:49.520
Ta-da! I'm thinking
of going to a movie with Sun-chan!

00:02:49.890 --> 00:02:51.730
I see. That's a good idea.

00:02:52.440 --> 00:02:53.310
I know, right?

00:02:53.690 --> 00:02:55.190
Here. I appreciate it.

00:02:55.190 --> 00:02:56.030
Excuse me?

00:02:56.030 --> 00:02:59.450
All you need to do
is make the plan with Sun-chan!

00:02:59.820 --> 00:03:04.330
S-So you want me to set up
a date between you two?

00:03:04.580 --> 00:03:06.660
Bingo! That's absolutely correct!

00:03:08.160 --> 00:03:12.120
- Why don't you ask him yourself?
- What? No way!

00:03:12.120 --> 00:03:14.840
<i>What? Are you an idiot?</i>

00:03:15.090 --> 00:03:16.460
B-But...

00:03:16.710 --> 00:03:18.840
Come on, please, Joro!

00:03:18.840 --> 00:03:21.430
<i>Bitch! Bitchier! Bitchiest!</i>

00:03:22.470 --> 00:03:24.550
It's definitely better if you ask him!

00:03:24.550 --> 00:03:26.810
After all, you guys are best friends!

00:03:27.850 --> 00:03:29.350
Best friends.

00:03:31.940 --> 00:03:33.850
Okay! Leave it to me!

00:03:33.850 --> 00:03:36.270
Yay! Thanks, Joro?

00:03:36.650 --> 00:03:37.610
A movie?

00:03:37.860 --> 00:03:40.820
Yeah. I happened to have two of them
in my hand.

00:03:41.780 --> 00:03:44.240
You want to hang out with me that badly?

00:03:45.160 --> 00:03:50.040
Actually, I've already seen this movie,
so why don't you go with someone else?

00:03:50.040 --> 00:03:51.460
For example, Himawari—

00:03:51.460 --> 00:03:52.410
Yay!

00:03:52.410 --> 00:03:53.790
I can't wait to see that movie!

00:03:53.790 --> 00:03:55.540
<i>That was too damn early!</i>

00:03:55.960 --> 00:03:58.170
Himawari, you want to see this movie?

00:03:58.170 --> 00:03:59.210
Yeah, I do!

00:03:59.210 --> 00:04:01.760
Then, I'll give you my ticket.

00:04:02.340 --> 00:04:05.720
Oh, you're so happy
that you're speechless, huh?

00:04:05.720 --> 00:04:07.180
But you should thank Joro.

00:04:08.310 --> 00:04:09.770
Joro.

00:04:09.770 --> 00:04:12.600
<i>I'm supposed to do something here?</i>

00:04:12.600 --> 00:04:16.440
Oh, in that case, why don't you two go?

00:04:16.440 --> 00:04:17.690
Me and Himawari?

00:04:18.190 --> 00:04:20.400
You two are so busy with your clubs,

00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:22.530
you hardly ever get
a chance to go somewhere.

00:04:22.860 --> 00:04:26.620
I agree! I haven't gone anywhere lately!

00:04:26.950 --> 00:04:28.330
<i>What about last time with me?</i>

00:04:30.120 --> 00:04:31.330
I see! Okay, sure!

00:04:32.200 --> 00:04:34.540
Then, why don't we go next Saturday?

00:04:34.540 --> 00:04:37.040
All right! Thank you, Sun-chan!

00:04:37.840 --> 00:04:39.090
You mean, "Thank you, Joro."

00:04:39.420 --> 00:04:41.960
It's okay! I already thanked him earlier!

00:04:43.340 --> 00:04:44.680
Earlier?

00:04:45.630 --> 00:04:48.890
I'm thinking of having lunch with Sun-chan!

00:04:49.260 --> 00:04:54.020
I understand. You brought homemade lunch,
so you want me to set up a situation

00:04:54.020 --> 00:04:58.400
where you and Sun-chan
would eat together, right?

00:04:58.690 --> 00:05:01.400
H-How did you know what my plan was?

00:05:01.730 --> 00:05:03.860
Because I just went through this
a few minutes ago.

00:05:04.240 --> 00:05:09.620
That's right. I figured you could do something
since you're best friends.

00:05:10.530 --> 00:05:12.040
Best friends.

00:05:15.120 --> 00:05:17.370
Okay. You can count on me.

00:05:17.370 --> 00:05:19.790
Really? Thank you, Joro!

00:05:20.710 --> 00:05:21.800
Sorry, Sun-chan,

00:05:22.090 --> 00:05:24.220
for making you help carry these files.

00:05:24.630 --> 00:05:27.970
No problem. You talk like we're strangers.

00:05:27.970 --> 00:05:29.890
We're buddies, aren't we?

00:05:38.730 --> 00:05:42.400
<i>The play is she starts
a natural conversation,</i>

00:05:42.400 --> 00:05:46.570
<i>and then I propose lunch
at an opportune moment.</i>

00:05:46.570 --> 00:05:48.360
Hey there, Cosmos.

00:05:48.700 --> 00:05:51.280
Well, greetings, Lord Oga.

00:05:53.160 --> 00:05:55.790
Such a fine day it is we're having.

00:05:55.790 --> 00:05:59.580
Indeed, I would partake of lunch
on the roof of this building.

00:05:59.580 --> 00:06:01.290
Why have you become a samurai?

00:06:01.750 --> 00:06:04.920
Um, is something wrong? Cosmos?

00:06:05.590 --> 00:06:08.260
Wrong? Nay, perish the thought!

00:06:10.550 --> 00:06:15.180
<i>Apparently, when she gets nervous,
she acts like some ersatz samurai.</i>

00:06:16.140 --> 00:06:18.480
Lord Kisaragi, I await your good offices.

00:06:18.480 --> 00:06:19.650
<i>I don't have any!</i>

00:06:20.150 --> 00:06:22.610
Oh, that, President Cosmos?

00:06:23.770 --> 00:06:26.320
Since you and Sun-chan have become friends,

00:06:26.320 --> 00:06:29.740
did you come here to invite him
to have lunch with you?

00:06:29.740 --> 00:06:30.740
Indeed, yes!

00:06:30.740 --> 00:06:32.780
Oh, that's what it is?

00:06:32.780 --> 00:06:35.490
The thing is, I either get lunch
from the co-op or the caf—

00:06:35.700 --> 00:06:37.500
Maybe it's okay!

00:06:37.500 --> 00:06:40.670
I understand that President Cosmos
always makes plenty.

00:06:40.670 --> 00:06:43.710
Aye, indeed!
You need not be concerned, Lord Oga.

00:06:43.880 --> 00:06:45.420
Really?

00:06:45.880 --> 00:06:49.680
Certainly! It includes one of your favorite,
deep-fried skewered pork!

00:06:49.680 --> 00:06:51.090
So, take it!

00:06:51.090 --> 00:06:52.930
Thanks, I'm starving!

00:06:52.930 --> 00:06:55.100
But then, let's share it with Joro, too!

00:06:56.810 --> 00:07:01.440
I-I actually have plans to meet another girl
during lunch, so I don't think I can make it.

00:07:01.810 --> 00:07:03.480
Really?

00:07:03.480 --> 00:07:06.230
Jeez, you're a smooth operator.

00:07:06.230 --> 00:07:08.490
So you two have lunch together!

00:07:08.490 --> 00:07:09.860
Okay, got it.

00:07:09.860 --> 00:07:11.610
And now I must take my leave!

00:07:13.240 --> 00:07:14.580
So that's what happened.

00:07:14.580 --> 00:07:16.910
At the moment,
it's going well for them, just barely.

00:07:17.160 --> 00:07:18.040
I see.

00:07:19.750 --> 00:07:22.500
I swear, they're both terrible at this.

00:07:22.500 --> 00:07:25.250
Though I do have to give them
points for diligence.

00:07:26.670 --> 00:07:28.590
But maybe...

00:07:29.510 --> 00:07:30.800
Got something to say?

00:07:31.130 --> 00:07:34.800
Something, but I don't have proof,
so I'll keep it to myself for now.

00:07:35.050 --> 00:07:37.560
Then, you shouldn't have said anything at all!

00:07:37.560 --> 00:07:41.640
No way. I want to talk to you, Joro,
even if only a little bit.

00:07:41.640 --> 00:07:45.560
I have to do my best, too,
so you can finish helping them.

00:07:49.070 --> 00:07:50.240
Look...

00:07:50.240 --> 00:07:51.320
Yes?

00:07:51.320 --> 00:07:53.410
Why are you doing this?

00:07:53.780 --> 00:07:57.620
Well, when it's all over,
we'll have more time to spend together.

00:07:57.950 --> 00:07:59.580
As if!

00:07:59.580 --> 00:08:02.410
When this is over,
I'm going to meet and make out

00:08:02.410 --> 00:08:06.340
with a nice, beautiful girl
with a big heart and bigger boobs...

00:08:06.750 --> 00:08:07.960
You mean me, then.

00:08:08.170 --> 00:08:11.470
You don't fit the bill at all,
you astoundingly ugly pig!

00:08:13.430 --> 00:08:15.430
By the way, one thing sticks out for me.

00:08:15.430 --> 00:08:16.260
What is it?

00:08:16.720 --> 00:08:19.600
You're helping two girls
try to get a boyfriend, right?

00:08:19.600 --> 00:08:21.270
Yeah, that's right.

00:08:21.560 --> 00:08:25.900
But what do you intend to do
if Oga likes a girl?

00:08:31.030 --> 00:08:32.440
Hadn't thought of that, huh?

00:08:32.990 --> 00:08:34.660
I-I didn't think of it.

00:08:34.660 --> 00:08:36.030
Are you grateful to me?

00:08:36.030 --> 00:08:37.490
N-Not especially.

00:08:37.490 --> 00:08:39.620
Aww, even after I did my best.

00:08:40.160 --> 00:08:43.290
All right! Yes! Fine!
I am grateful! Thank you!

00:08:43.290 --> 00:08:45.000
Then I want a reward.

00:08:46.000 --> 00:08:47.960
What do you want me to do?

00:08:48.210 --> 00:08:50.380
The student council's library inspection.

00:08:50.880 --> 00:08:52.920
I wonder who's going to do that.

00:08:55.430 --> 00:08:56.840
I'll think about it.

00:08:57.970 --> 00:09:00.560
<i>A girl who Sun-chan likes.</i>

00:09:00.560 --> 00:09:02.850
<i>I've gotta look into that.</i>

00:09:08.480 --> 00:09:11.320
Awesome! It's like Sun-chan never misses.

00:09:12.190 --> 00:09:13.490
Hey, Sun-chan.

00:09:14.200 --> 00:09:15.030
What's up, Joro?

00:09:15.490 --> 00:09:16.740
Is there someone you like?

00:09:21.290 --> 00:09:23.870
Wh-Where's that coming from?

00:09:24.540 --> 00:09:25.370
There is, huh?

00:09:29.250 --> 00:09:30.090
I guess.

00:09:30.460 --> 00:09:33.960
Is it all right for me to ask who it is?

00:09:33.960 --> 00:09:36.380
Sure. We're best friends, after all.

00:09:36.380 --> 00:09:38.680
You're the one person I don't mind telling.

00:09:38.680 --> 00:09:39.510
Thanks.

00:09:40.010 --> 00:09:42.220
But there are other people around.

00:09:46.390 --> 00:09:47.480
Why don't we talk there?

00:09:52.530 --> 00:09:55.990
<i>Wh-Why is there a bench?</i>

00:09:55.990 --> 00:09:58.660
<i>Why does there have to be a bench there?</i>

00:09:59.070 --> 00:10:03.660
<i>Think! Every time that bastard shows up,
I'm flung to the depths of despair!</i>

00:10:03.660 --> 00:10:05.540
<i>In other words, this time,</i>

00:10:04.830 --> 00:10:05.910
GIRLS WITH FLOWER NICKNAMES SO FAR!

00:10:05.540 --> 00:10:09.420
<i>don't tell me Sun-chan is in love with...</i>

00:10:05.910 --> 00:10:09.420
HIMAWARI

00:10:06.290 --> 00:10:09.420
COSMOS

00:10:09.920 --> 00:10:14.380
Um, first, would you sit next to me?

00:10:14.670 --> 00:10:19.090
<i>Don't say that line. No way. I can't...</i>

00:10:22.050 --> 00:10:25.600
Actually, the girl I really like...

00:10:27.180 --> 00:10:31.440
Whenever I think about her,
I get a tightness in my chest.

00:10:31.440 --> 00:10:34.980
But I'm happy
just getting to see her every day.

00:10:35.440 --> 00:10:40.950
<i>Got it. I'm an authority
on hearing people's confessions of love.</i>

00:10:41.320 --> 00:10:43.410
I-I...

00:10:47.040 --> 00:10:49.830
I'm in love with Sumireko Sanshokuin!

00:10:51.130 --> 00:10:53.290
<i>Why did it have to be her?</i>

00:10:53.880 --> 00:10:58.380
It all started last year at the final game
of the regional baseball tournament.

00:10:58.380 --> 00:10:59.760
<i>You're stuck on that, too?</i>

00:11:00.260 --> 00:11:06.100
My last pitch for that game,
my control was off a bit.

00:11:06.100 --> 00:11:08.770
If I'd only used my rosin bag then.

00:11:09.270 --> 00:11:11.730
Yeah, I was there, too.

00:11:11.940 --> 00:11:18.240
So I held back in front of everyone, but once
I was alone, I couldn't take it anymore,

00:11:18.240 --> 00:11:20.650
and this is embarrassing, but I cried.

00:11:20.650 --> 00:11:23.660
I just didn't want anyone to see me like that.

00:11:24.070 --> 00:11:28.410
<i>Strange. He already had
two witnesses, east and west.</i>

00:11:28.410 --> 00:11:31.210
I went out the south exit,
which is the least crowded.

00:11:31.670 --> 00:11:34.380
<i>Take this Southern belle to Koshien!</i>

00:11:34.670 --> 00:11:38.300
And that's where I met her!
Sanshokuin!

00:11:38.800 --> 00:11:40.340
Even now, I remember it well.

00:11:41.430 --> 00:11:44.680
"A guy like you, who's kind,
strong, does his best,

00:11:44.680 --> 00:11:48.470
and holds back tears in front of people
is sure to win next time."

00:11:48.720 --> 00:11:50.850
That's what she said to me!

00:11:52.190 --> 00:11:53.810
<i>What the hell is she doing?</i>

00:11:54.230 --> 00:11:58.440
So I know this is pathetic,
but since I told you this much, I'll say it.

00:11:58.900 --> 00:12:02.320
Joro, would you help
me and Sanshokuin get together?

00:12:04.320 --> 00:12:06.700
Sorry. I can't do that.

00:12:07.540 --> 00:12:12.160
<i>Even though Sun-chan is asking me for a favor,
if they found out, they'd kill me!</i>

00:12:12.460 --> 00:12:14.670
Don't be like that! Please help me!

00:12:14.670 --> 00:12:16.960
I know you get along with Sanshokuin—

00:12:16.960 --> 00:12:22.010
I've hardly ever talked to her,
and we don't especially get along.

00:12:24.220 --> 00:12:25.260
All right.

00:12:25.680 --> 00:12:27.560
Well, should we go back?

00:12:28.140 --> 00:12:29.850
Can I ask you one thing?

00:12:30.390 --> 00:12:31.230
What is it?

00:12:31.770 --> 00:12:34.730
It's a big moment, where,
if the other team gets a hit, you lose.

00:12:34.730 --> 00:12:39.440
Their fourth batter is at bat. What do you do?

00:12:39.440 --> 00:12:41.690
Should you walk him intentionally?

00:12:42.070 --> 00:12:44.950
<i>Sun-chan really is a baseball fanatic.</i>

00:12:45.450 --> 00:12:49.330
Well, if it were me, maybe I would walk him.

00:12:49.330 --> 00:12:51.410
But that's not you, right, Sun-chan?

00:12:51.910 --> 00:12:52.750
It's not me?

00:12:53.210 --> 00:12:54.830
Faith and effort.

00:12:54.830 --> 00:12:57.590
Believing in what you
and your teammates have been doing.

00:12:57.590 --> 00:13:00.170
Never running away,
but pitching for all you're worth.

00:13:00.170 --> 00:13:01.460
That's who you are, Sun-chan.

00:13:02.420 --> 00:13:04.930
You're right. Yeah, you're right!

00:13:05.260 --> 00:13:07.930
You don't know how happy
it makes me to hear that!

00:13:09.890 --> 00:13:11.890
<i>I have two choices.</i>

00:13:12.180 --> 00:13:15.900
<i>The first one
is to keep helping Himawari and Cosmos.</i>

00:13:15.900 --> 00:13:19.360
<i>But, when I think about Sun-chan's feelings,
there's the other choice.</i>

00:13:22.570 --> 00:13:25.070
I'm thrilled that you wanted to see me.

00:13:25.530 --> 00:13:28.200
H-Hi, Sanshokuin.

00:13:28.200 --> 00:13:30.120
Sorry to suddenly call you out here.

00:13:30.780 --> 00:13:33.700
All right, fine.
I understand that people can see us here.

00:13:34.000 --> 00:13:35.750
So what did you want?

00:13:37.080 --> 00:13:38.170
U-Um, listen.

00:13:38.580 --> 00:13:42.050
Maybe you had a taste for the cookies
I baked that you refused to eat at lun—

00:13:42.050 --> 00:13:43.840
What do you think about Sun-chan?

00:13:47.970 --> 00:13:49.430
What does that mean?

00:13:49.760 --> 00:13:51.850
Just what I said.

00:13:51.850 --> 00:13:53.600
So that's what it is?

00:13:53.600 --> 00:13:56.520
Forget it. Whatever you're thinking, I refuse.

00:13:56.520 --> 00:13:59.900
Don't be so hasty. You could just try it once.

00:14:00.360 --> 00:14:03.730
There's no point.
There's only one person I want to be with,

00:14:03.730 --> 00:14:05.900
and he's standing
right in front of me.

00:14:06.240 --> 00:14:07.400
<i>I...</i>

00:14:07.910 --> 00:14:10.910
I want you to be with someone else.

00:14:12.280 --> 00:14:13.910
I want to be with you.

00:14:13.910 --> 00:14:17.870
Oh, come on. I mean, compared to me,
Sun-chan is much more—

00:14:18.920 --> 00:14:20.130
That's enough!

00:14:21.460 --> 00:14:24.840
What's going on?
Did he just ask Sanshokuin out?

00:14:24.840 --> 00:14:26.220
Talk about bad taste.

00:14:26.220 --> 00:14:27.760
<i>I agree!</i>

00:14:27.760 --> 00:14:31.140
How could you say something so cruel?

00:14:31.760 --> 00:14:37.940
When all I want is to talk to you
and eat yummy cookies together.

00:14:37.940 --> 00:14:39.690
- L-Look, Pan—
- Yo!

00:14:39.690 --> 00:14:42.900
Joro, what are you up to?

00:14:44.480 --> 00:14:46.940
Why are you with Sanshokuin? Don't tell me.

00:14:47.190 --> 00:14:49.450
W-Wait! Sun-chan,
it's not what you think! There's nothing—

00:14:49.450 --> 00:14:51.820
You told me you didn't
especially get along with her!

00:14:51.820 --> 00:14:52.660
Um...

00:14:53.120 --> 00:14:54.120
Uh, this is...

00:14:54.490 --> 00:14:58.120
Hey, say something.
We're best friends, aren't we?

00:15:00.040 --> 00:15:03.500
Joro came to tell me something
about student council, right?

00:15:04.630 --> 00:15:08.050
There's a library inspection after school today.

00:15:08.050 --> 00:15:10.430
I expect you came to inform me about that.

00:15:10.760 --> 00:15:12.680
Th-That's right!

00:15:12.680 --> 00:15:15.970
I'm in charge of that,
so I thought, if I told her in advance,

00:15:15.970 --> 00:15:17.520
we could do it more efficiently!

00:15:18.390 --> 00:15:21.770
<i>I didn't think she would throw me a life jacket!</i>

00:15:21.770 --> 00:15:24.230
But it looked more serious than that.

00:15:24.230 --> 00:15:29.240
Not many people use the library,
so there's talk of closing it.

00:15:29.610 --> 00:15:30.990
Oh, that's what it was.

00:15:30.990 --> 00:15:33.620
Well, I'm heading back.

00:15:33.620 --> 00:15:34.830
Okay.

00:15:34.830 --> 00:15:36.240
Wait, Sanshokuin!

00:15:36.830 --> 00:15:37.660
Yes?

00:15:37.660 --> 00:15:44.000
Um, so the only connection between you and
Joro is student council and library aide, right?

00:15:44.000 --> 00:15:44.840
No.

00:15:46.250 --> 00:15:49.920
Apparently it's student council
and library aide who don't get along.

00:15:52.430 --> 00:15:56.350
Goodbye, unfriendly, rude jerk Joro.

00:16:02.440 --> 00:16:04.060
Sorry I was suspicious of you, Joro.

00:16:04.060 --> 00:16:06.020
L-Listen, Sun-chan.

00:16:06.020 --> 00:16:09.070
It's okay! I understand.

00:16:14.240 --> 00:16:15.370
GEEZ, YOU JUST WANT TO REALLY SEE ME, DON'T YOU?
YOU SHOULD BE MORE UPFRONT ABOUT IT <3

00:16:15.370 --> 00:16:17.450
<i>For now,
you don't have to come to the library.</i>

00:16:18.870 --> 00:16:21.290
<i>I guess she's still mad.</i>

00:16:21.290 --> 00:16:23.830
<i>But start coming again next week on Monday.</i>

00:16:24.670 --> 00:16:27.710
<i>Maybe something interesting will happen
between now and then.</i>

00:16:27.710 --> 00:16:29.920
<i>Fine. Also...</i>

00:16:30.420 --> 00:16:32.130
YES?

00:16:32.130 --> 00:16:34.890
THE COOKIES WERE GOOD...

00:16:33.930 --> 00:16:37.180
<i>I didn't go back to the library
for the next several days,</i>

00:16:37.180 --> 00:16:40.060
<i>but spent my free time
supporting Cosmos and Himawari.</i>

00:16:40.390 --> 00:16:43.850
<i>I arranged it so Cosmos and Sun-chan
would walk home together today.</i>

00:16:44.440 --> 00:16:47.770
<i>Tomorrow's Saturday, the day
of Himawari and Sun-chan's movie date.</i>

00:16:48.270 --> 00:16:50.530
<i>I hope one of them works out well.</i>

00:16:52.070 --> 00:16:54.530
SAKURA AKINO
DO YOU HAVE ANY FREE TIME TOMORROW?

00:16:54.910 --> 00:16:57.070
Such a deceptively simple sentence.

00:16:57.580 --> 00:16:59.990
Did something happen today?

00:17:02.830 --> 00:17:05.670
<i>Okay, where's Cosmos?</i>

00:17:06.960 --> 00:17:08.630
Found her.

00:17:12.760 --> 00:17:13.590
Um...

00:17:15.050 --> 00:17:17.550
Hi, Joro.

00:17:18.550 --> 00:17:19.970
D-Did something happen?

00:17:19.970 --> 00:17:20.890
Actually...

00:17:24.440 --> 00:17:30.400
Sun-chan asked me to help him
get close to Sumireko Sanshokuin.

00:17:31.820 --> 00:17:35.280
Apparently, as the president of student council,
I have a magnetic personality,

00:17:35.280 --> 00:17:39.950
which I can use to get close to Sanshokuin,
so he wants my help with her.

00:17:39.950 --> 00:17:41.490
R-Really?

00:17:42.410 --> 00:17:45.460
You knew how he felt, didn't you?

00:17:47.830 --> 00:17:50.170
Yes. I knew.

00:17:51.710 --> 00:17:54.130
Why didn't you tell me?

00:17:54.550 --> 00:17:58.220
I couldn't, knowing how you felt about him.

00:17:58.550 --> 00:18:00.180
Is that the truth?

00:18:01.970 --> 00:18:04.020
This is what Sun-chan said.

00:18:04.020 --> 00:18:05.680
"When I asked Joro for advice,

00:18:05.680 --> 00:18:10.060
he told me to work with friends who I trust
and challenge my limits

00:18:10.060 --> 00:18:12.400
and, with love and baseball,
you give it all you got."

00:18:13.780 --> 00:18:15.490
That's why he asked for my help!

00:18:15.490 --> 00:18:17.610
I didn't say any of that!

00:18:17.610 --> 00:18:19.620
Stop lying to me.

00:18:19.990 --> 00:18:22.870
He said that when he
gave you an example in baseball terms,

00:18:22.870 --> 00:18:24.750
you gave him a thoughtful answer.

00:18:27.040 --> 00:18:30.290
<i>No, Sun-chan! That's not what I meant!</i>

00:18:30.290 --> 00:18:31.960
It seems you know what I'm talking about.

00:18:32.380 --> 00:18:35.340
U-Um, it's a misunderstanding!

00:18:35.340 --> 00:18:37.380
Another lie? I'm disappointed in you.

00:18:37.760 --> 00:18:40.590
<i>No! It's the truth! I didn't mean it like that!</i>

00:18:41.100 --> 00:18:42.930
I don't need you anymore.

00:18:42.930 --> 00:18:45.850
I'm helping Sun-chan get a girlfriend now.

00:18:47.770 --> 00:18:51.770
Goodbye, insensitive, cruel jerk Joro.

00:18:57.570 --> 00:19:01.910
Against the words of the guy
she's in love with, I can't win.

00:19:03.700 --> 00:19:07.160
AOI HINATA
CAN I SEE YOU TOMORROW?

00:19:08.000 --> 00:19:11.130
<i>Is this... Seriously?</i>

00:19:13.380 --> 00:19:18.590
I'm so cheerful and funny that it'd be easy
for me to get close to Sanshokuin,

00:19:18.590 --> 00:19:20.470
so he wants my help with her.

00:19:20.800 --> 00:19:22.220
<i>I knew it.</i>

00:19:22.600 --> 00:19:27.520
<i>How could he ask Himawari
and Cosmos the same favor?</i>

00:19:27.520 --> 00:19:28.390
Why?

00:19:29.770 --> 00:19:31.520
Why didn't you tell me...

00:19:32.230 --> 00:19:33.980
how Sun-chan felt?

00:19:34.940 --> 00:19:38.740
Sorry. Knowing how you felt,
I couldn't tell you.

00:19:38.740 --> 00:19:41.700
<i>I'm not going to make the same mistake
that I did with Cosmos!</i>

00:19:42.240 --> 00:19:46.080
Also, to be honest,
Sun-chan asked me for my advice, too,

00:19:46.080 --> 00:19:49.410
but, when I answered him,
I thought he was talking about baseball.

00:19:49.410 --> 00:19:50.330
Sorry.

00:19:50.330 --> 00:19:51.170
Liar.

00:19:52.170 --> 00:19:53.500
Sun-chan told me!

00:19:53.790 --> 00:19:55.790
"Joro is an awesome best friend.

00:19:55.790 --> 00:19:58.710
Even when I pretended
to be talking about baseball,

00:19:58.710 --> 00:20:00.470
he knew it was a metaphor for love!"

00:20:00.720 --> 00:20:02.720
<i>How could he get that messed up?</i>

00:20:02.890 --> 00:20:06.850
- That's wrong! I never meant it like—
- You're lying! That's what Sun-chan told me!

00:20:07.310 --> 00:20:10.680
<i>Why doesn't anyone believe what I'm saying?</i>

00:20:11.060 --> 00:20:12.650
<i>Why?</i>

00:20:12.650 --> 00:20:14.940
Please, Himawari, listen to—

00:20:18.070 --> 00:20:20.240
I'm going to help Sun-chan!

00:20:20.240 --> 00:20:22.530
- So I don't need you, Joro!
- Ow!

00:20:22.530 --> 00:20:25.660
Bye, mean, lying jerk Joro!

00:20:31.160 --> 00:20:35.920
Two important relationships
right out the window.

00:20:50.560 --> 00:20:52.180
Hey, Joro!

00:20:53.190 --> 00:20:54.560
You need something?

00:20:54.560 --> 00:20:59.020
No, you just haven't seemed
like yourself since this morning.

00:20:59.610 --> 00:21:01.030
Sun-chan.

00:21:01.030 --> 00:21:04.360
Look, if something's bugging you,
let me be your sounding board.

00:21:04.360 --> 00:21:06.570
What are friends for, right?

00:21:06.570 --> 00:21:10.290
Yeah. If it gets any worse,
I might take you up on that offer.

00:21:10.290 --> 00:21:12.750
Okay. You know where to find me.

00:21:14.750 --> 00:21:17.460
TODAY IS "NEXT WEEK'S MONDAY"

00:21:15.710 --> 00:21:17.460
I know.

00:21:19.130 --> 00:21:20.420
What do you want?

00:21:20.670 --> 00:21:23.130
That's not the way to talk
when you came on your own.

00:21:23.130 --> 00:21:24.430
You called me here.

00:21:25.130 --> 00:21:28.140
Right. It's gotten more interesting, hasn't it?

00:21:29.600 --> 00:21:33.180
You worked so hard to support those two
with their quest for love,

00:21:33.180 --> 00:21:34.560
but it all went up in smoke.

00:21:35.140 --> 00:21:36.940
In the end, it was a waste of time.

00:21:36.940 --> 00:21:38.020
You...

00:21:38.440 --> 00:21:42.150
Even though neither of them stand a chance
of their feelings being reciprocated,

00:21:42.150 --> 00:21:44.740
they have to stand by the person they love.

00:21:45.070 --> 00:21:47.410
They have to continue to support him.

00:21:47.410 --> 00:21:49.370
I really feel sorry for them.

00:21:49.370 --> 00:21:50.950
That's enough out of you.

00:21:50.950 --> 00:21:54.290
But the most interesting thing, Joro...

00:22:00.040 --> 00:22:02.000
is what happens next.

00:23:34.930 --> 00:23:39.940
EPISODE 03
I MET YOU BEFORE

00:23:36.220 --> 00:23:38.230
I met you before.
